      "attack_scenario": "Attacker shares a crafted level file (e.g. 'Original1.cheat') with a player, or drops it into the game's working directory under levels/. The file contains a valid serialization stream header (AC ED 00 05) followed by block data whose first two ints are, e.g., 0x40000000 x 0x40000000. When the victim starts the game or opens the file via Load, readLevel attempts to allocate ~2^60 ints and the JVM dies with OutOfMemoryError; a negative dimension instead throws NegativeArraySizeException, which is not caught (readLevel only catches EOFException and IOException, lines 479-487) and propagates up through load(), crashing the game on the event/init thread. Moderate dimensions (e.g. 200000x200000) hang or exhaust the heap. Gained: denial of service of the victim's game process; no code execution is possible because only primitive reads are performed.",
