  "categI have now reviewed the whole variant. Summary of what I verified:

- All 59 files enumerated; every file content-searched for network, file, reflection, deserialization, native, and crypto sinks; the ~15 security-relevant files read line-by-line.
- **No** `ObjectInputStream`, **no** `System.load`/JNI, **no** `user.home`/`user.dir` paths, **no** `Runtime.exec`, **no** hardcoded credentials.
- `ApoClassLoader` (URLClassLoader + `newInstance`) and `ApoIO` (custom binary level I/O) exist as cloned shared infrastructure but are **never instantiated/subclassed** in this variant — levels are procedurally generated (`ApoJumpLevel.makePlatforms`), so the custom-parser-over-files category is dead code here.
- Real attack surface: plain-HTTP highscore get/save, plain-HTTP "cookies.php" achievement channel (applet mode only), and a naive remote-response parser feeding into game state. `ApoHelp.getMd5Digest` exists but is **never called** — highscore submissions carry no integrity token at all.

